  backtrack
place tren
  # tren, whose e is open where the -ent words' is not: gent, cent and vent
  # are e-n-t and this asks for a word that ends at the n. The letter in front
  # is asked about for the same reason the -on arm asks: ben is close. Every
  # verb that ends in -ren -- corren, obren, entren -- has the e unstressed
  # there, and an unstressed open e is a schwa by the time it is spoken, so
